From 0010-nouveau-gr-idle-gate Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0010/0010] nouveau: gate runtime suspend on GR idle

Cutting the power of the GT 750M while the graphics engine is still busy
leaves the Kepler card in an unrecoverable state: the gmux power-cut is
deeper than D3cold, and a mid-render cut makes the device impossible to
re-initialize on resume (raport 22 section B.4).  The NVIDIA blob's dynamic-PM
state machine never drops power while a client is active.

Expose the existing GF100+ GR idle test as nvkm_gr_wait_idle() and gate
nouveau_pmops_runtime_suspend() on it: if GR is busy or a context switch
is in progress the function waits up to 2 s; if GR still is not idle it
returns -EBUSY and the runtime PM core retries after the autosuspend
delay instead of cutting power mid-render.

Older (pre-Fermi) chips are left alone: they report busy through the same
0x40060c bit but expose no context-switch-in-progress state, so the test
is not reliable for them.

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvkm/engine/gr.h |    1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c   |   16 ++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c            |   14 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvkm/engine/gr.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvkm/engine/gr.h
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 
 u64 nvkm_gr_units(struct nvkm_gr *);
 int nvkm_gr_tlb_flush(struct nvkm_gr *);
+int nvkm_gr_wait_idle(struct nvkm_gr *);
 int nvkm_gr_ctxsw_pause(struct nvkm_device *);
 int nvkm_gr_ctxsw_resume(struct nvkm_device *);
 u32 nvkm_gr_ctxsw_inst(struct nvkm_device *);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/gr/gf100.c
@@ -1075,6 +1075,22 @@
 	return -EAGAIN;
 }
 
+int
+nvkm_gr_wait_idle(struct nvkm_gr *gr)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Wait for the graphics engine to go idle.  Only GF100+ expose the
+	 * context-switch-in-progress state that makes the test reliable;
+	 * older chips report busy through the same 0x40060c bit but cannot
+	 * distinguish a mid-context-switch from a real idle, so leave them
+	 * alone.
+	 */
+	if (gr->engine.subdev.device->card_type < NV_C0)
+		return 0;
+
+	return gf100_gr_wait_idle(gf100_gr(gr));
+}
+
 void
 gf100_gr_mmio(struct gf100_gr *gr, const struct gf100_gr_pack *p)
 {
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
@@ -1156,6 +1156,20 @@
 	}
 
 	nouveau_switcheroo_optimus_dsm();
+	/* Refuse to cut power while the GPU is still busy: a hard power-cut
+	 * (gmux rails) with GR busy leaves the device in an unrecoverable
+	 * state on Kepler.  Wait for GR to go idle and, if it never does,
+	 * bail out; the runtime PM core will retry after the autosuspend
+	 * delay.
+	 */
+	if (nvxx_gr(drm)) {
+		ret = nvkm_gr_wait_idle(nvxx_gr(drm));
+		if (ret) {
+			NV_DEBUG(drm, "GR not idle, deferring runtime suspend\n");
+			return -EBUSY;
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = nouveau_do_suspend(drm, true);
 	pci_save_state(pdev);
 	pci_disable_device(pdev);
